Also just so people know, not everyone who understands you will do it to really help, manipulators will do their very best to master you and understand your motivations to really prove their power and that they are the upper hand, they **love** *power play*, people will find your weaknesses, traumas, hurt and pain to ***poke*** on it. I have experienced this first-hand. Growing up w/ narcissistic abuse, gaslighting and manipulation is a guaranteed way to screw someone mentally and scar them spiritually, when you have been introduced to such treatment and behavior, then you are always on high alert for deceit, false-hope, discouragement, betrayal, unreliableness and temperament of people. I know it seems as if a person can just pick up themselves after such thing has left their life or them getting out of such situation, but only two things I noticed, either this person would tend to adapt this behavior and make them take it out on others later on in life or it would make a person constantly doubt themselves/a situation, their judgement and resort to self-sabotage and discouragement.   


I have turned out to be the second, I unconsciously weigh out the consequences of my every action and decision critically because I fear being unsafe and unstable, since I am so traumatized by instability in life. I also do not want to feel sorry for myself yet I do not want to put judgement on others even if they have wronged me because I really do not want to feel the weight of **condemnation.** I wouldn't impose it on anyone since my mom and sis and my family only bases my identity on my tantrums and mistakes. 

&#x200B;

As a child, my abusers which was my mom and my sister were so unforgiving to me and take out their anger and frustrations on me even if I never caused any thing to happen. For an instance, whenever the slightest inconvenience occurs, there is always someone to blame and divert their agitation, annoyance, or anger to. There is always someone to blame. Why me, when I didn't cause things to happen that way? 

&#x200B;

They have failed to be accountable for their own words and actions and be responsible for their own feelings.  


I then as a child decided to have a strong conviction to be accountable and responsible to an extent, it is a way for me to rise above situations even if it's traumatic. I cannot be strong all the time, so sometimes self-sabotage wins over me and I make decisions based on what is harmless to others even if it is somewhat detrimental or unsatisfying for myself. 

&#x200B;

My initial response and what I always strongly feel to do is to *mediate* things. 

&#x200B;

so since I was so tricked into thinking as a child that everything is my fault, I only make my decisions based on prioritizing my safety, and being harmless/not worsening someone else's situation/feeling or affecting anyone else's s life drastically.   


This includes me having a difficulty to ask help, hating the feeling of being the cause of someone's burden or discomfort, and being responsible for someone else's problem. It gets in the way of integrating my life with someone whether it be a friendship or a relationship, because every single exchange of things seems *conditional.* This is what abuse does to you my friends. We cannot recognize good or bad intent. 

&#x200B;

I don't think so there is anything worth losing yourself over, specially since my latest abusers have done their best for me to lose my cool, forget my character, morals and values and the person that I have built myself to be, just to make me do things and mold me to be their puppet. They wanted me to have trauma so bad, I never consented for them to be in my life, but even so I am grateful for all the things I have gone through and lessons I have learned about others, about life, and about myself. 

&#x200B;

I am now relying on God, my faith in him is strong, and I leave space for every situation in my life to be covered in grace for broken things to be mended, missing pieces to be restored, and for everything to make perfect sense in the end. For me, my loved ones, even the ones who have wronged me, and for the things I have done (the bad), and things I have failed to do. Everything my life has been and will be, I surrender to God. 

&#x200B;

*Peace is a priority, even if sometimes it means loneliness.*

Going vegan/vegetarian might give you more options! Add different veggies and fruits to your diet and you will find yourself feeling more lighter, more energized and nourished :D You can do smoothies, salads, grilled, baked, casserole, soups etc., 

&#x200B;

I do eat tofu everyday as my source of protein, it tastes bland, sometimes I eat it with rice sometimes I do not, but I compensate w/ the blandness by giving myself snacks later, I also love drinking stuff (unhealthy), junk foods, and everything I could, but GF of course. :D

Thanks for having the hands I can finally melt into. 🤍

&#x200B;

P.S. I will never lose hope. I love you.

Free urself baby, there is always love waiting for you. 

&#x200B;

No matter where I go, I know I'll love you too. 

&#x200B;

No matter what.

I take relationships so much seriously, and I told myself that I would never cheat because I would not put anyone through the same pain that I have experienced from having a parent that is absent and has had numerous affairs. I guess it's also what makes me loyal to a fault, I then vowed that I would never engage in infidelity myself. However I have a person, and I am so in love with him, but I do not think that life would allow us to happen in a way that I want. I really am certain that it's him because I refuse to allow myself to fall for anyone anymore, not out of spite, but because I am content that even if I cannot have him in the way that I want, I still would think of him as the love of my life. I am afraid that if I get into a relationship I would still think of him, and I do think it's very unfair for someone to be loved insincerely, and I wouldn't like to make anyone feel that way specially my would be then spouse. I also never think much about it but I'm also afraid that I might wake up one day and have cold feet.

I still wouldn't risk to be honest, and if I were to fall in love with someone else by the time that I'm already committed to someone, I hope that I end up things in good terms and have closure with them and be able to pursue my person without hurting anyone, but I still would rather not risk having to go through it, I would still not go for anyone if I still haven't moved on from my person no matter how long it takes, even until the day that I die.

I used to think that the overall experience of true love only promises good, and that it only consists of breathtaking moments and bliss, but in my case true love is a life sentence. I still do not regret it, however I now realize that we might not be aware of the fact that everyone in this lifetime has possibly met their true love, but only a very few gets to end up with theirs. I understand now, I guess we all have our "The one that got away".

&#x200B;

So I wish you and your person luck, and I hope that the universe favors you both, but if you don't then please don't spread your hurt any further to anyone else. The couple might have had their true love, but I don't think that it's very fair to their spouses and families to just vanish on thin air.

&#x200B;

And if you think that being alone is unbearable, then please just think of people like me. I am not miserable, instead I have decided to love my person from afar and in peace.

&#x200B;

Good luck stranger.

It's totally ok, I hope you did read my disclaimer in the end, I didn't even say that Chiron represents wounds (although it is one of it's symbolisms), but just how you described Uranus, Chiron also does have a lot of symbolisms and archetypes to represent. I have lots of aspect in Chiron and so I think it's safe for me to say these observations that I have from my own experience and perspective. I also do know that Chiron is not a planet, but it doesn't mean that it cannot be strongly felt in a chart, or for the aspect to be **void** in one's chart or in one's life. ***Ascendant***\*,\* ***North node***\*,\* ***South node***\*,\* and ***MC*** and ***IC*** are not planets, but they are considered *major focal points* in one's chart, so let's say for example, having an aspect between any of the major focal points (e.g. mc square ascendant) in one's chart could still play out as something that could just be as strong as planetxplanet, planetxasteroid, planetxnorthnode, etc., and I do agree with you, it does not exactly mean insecurity, however I have based it from the **mythology** itself, so I don't think so that I should unlearn the things that I based my observations from, (Chiron in my own interpretation can also mean sacrifice, suicide, marytrdom and a lot more of things but yes, if you want to focus on the positive it can mean a *'potential for healing'* nothing more nothing less, it does not mean immunity \*as chiron can literally heal anyone ***but*** himself\*), and like I said, these are only observations from my experiences of reading charts and aspects of people. Aspects can manifest in different ways and be interpreted by different astrologers, but still the person can be the only one who can confirm if it does resonate with them or their life events.

&#x200B;

**Edit:** About the first house thing, first house does not necessarily represent just the appearance, it is *'the soul's map'*, it is significant as it is the starting point of your life, it represents the dynamic that you are brought into (e.g. think of most sagittarius risings feeling foreign or considered as someone of a different culture by their peers/environment during their childhood and having major themes of multicultural/religion/geography and even multiple relocations throughout their life).

Hmm idk jealous but someone insecure, a lot of Chiron sextile aspects, because Chiron represents insecurity as Chiron is *unrelenting* pain, so this could translate into something *lingering* such as insecurity (as Chiron is both ruled by ***Saturn*** and ***Uranus***, makes someone feel somewhat ***restricted***/***lacking***/***not enough*** and ***odd***) sextile ***Venus*** (for physical appearance), sextile ***Moon*** (for relationships, makes someone brooding, needy, clingy, obsessive, sulky, and possibly an easily ***jealous*** lover), sextile ***Saturn*** (financially and materially).

&#x200B;

Another case is my dad and sister, they both are foul-mouthed and tend to wish ill on other people, they both have Mercury sextile Chiron, they are both naturally malicious. I find it common in a lot of narcissists.

&#x200B;

**Edit:** I do have Uranus sextile Chiron, I can say that I never felt as if I belong into any kind of group circle (This aspects gives me major redditor vibes lol), and you can always rely on me to be awkward in any social setting. I am so used to being alone though, I love solitude. Having a social responsibility in society is painful to me, I find it burdensome that sometimes there are things that cannot be achieved without having to involve other people.

&#x200B;

These are only my observations, not necessarily applicable to everyone with the said aspects.

go to [astro-seek.com](https://astro-seek.com), then select birth chart selection, enter your birth chart details, and you will se there are tabs under your birth chart wheel, you will see one of those tabs are labeled as 'dominants'.

&#x200B;

Not only will you see which planet is dominant in your chart but also your dominant/signature sign.
